---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/base';
---
<Guide
  title="Signing in to your website"
  heading="Signing in to"
  thin="your website."
  intro="Your website has a back room where you can change your own hours, add photos of finished jobs, and read the inquiries people send you. Here is how to get in the first time."
  description="How to sign in to your Weaver Digital website, set your password, and make your first change."
>
  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>We never send you a password.</strong> We send you a link, and you choose your own password on the other side of it. Nobody here ever knows what it is.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="steps">
    <div class="step reveal">
      <h2>Open the link we sent you</h2>
      <p>It arrives by text or email, and looks something like <code>my.weaverdigital.io/invite/…</code>. Open it on your phone or your computer, whichever you'd rather use.</p>
      <p>Can't find it? Just ask and we'll send another — it takes us a few seconds.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step reveal">
      <h2>Choose a password</h2>
      <p>Type a password you'll remember and press the button. That's the whole thing. Write it down somewhere you'll find it again.</p>
      <div class="note warn">
        <p>The link works <strong>once</strong>, and lasts about a week. If it has gone stale by the time you get to it, tell us — we can usually make the link you already have work again, so there's nothing new to go hunting for.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="step reveal">
      <h2>Bookmark the sign-in page</h2>
      <p>From then on, this is the only address you need:</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-blue" href="https://my.weaverdigital.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          my.weaverdigital.io <span class="arrow">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p>It works just as well on your phone as on a computer, so you can add a photo from a job while you're still standing in front of it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step reveal">
      <h2>Have a look around</h2>
      <p>Signing in drops you on your own dashboard. The thing to notice is the <strong>Needs you</strong> area at the top — anything waiting on you shows up there, so if that part is empty, nothing is on fire.</p>
      <p>Down the side you'll find the parts of your site you can change. Which ones you have depends on what we built — usually your services, a gallery of finished work, and customer reviews.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step reveal">
      <h2>Make a change</h2>
      <p>Pick any section, open an item, and edit it like you would a form. Add a new one with the button at the top of the list.</p>
      <p>When you save, your website rebuilds itself and your change appears publicly a few minutes later. There's no separate publish button to forget about, and nothing you can break by trying.</p>
      <div class="note">
        <p><strong>Photos are the thing worth doing.</strong> A gallery of real finished jobs does more for winning work than anything else you can change in here. Take the picture before you pack the van.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-section">
    <h2>If you get locked out later</h2>
    <p>Once you've set a password, you don't need us for this. Use <strong>Forgot your password?</strong> on the sign-in page and it'll email you a link to pick a new one.</p>
    <p>That's also the answer if your invite link says it has already been used — that message means your password is set, so the forgot-password link is the way back in.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="guide-section">
    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <p>While you're in there, it's worth two minutes making sure you get an email when somebody asks you for a price. That's the <a href={url('/guides/estimate-requests')}>next guide</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Guide>
